# World VFX (Echo and Shared Paths)

**`main`-mod** concern (`UseContext` / EchoBoss; not in base `master`). Any combat, ability, spell, item, or move that shows world VFX must work for **Hero and on-stage Echo**. Do not gate attack / jump / zap / MagicMissile / MissileSprite / operate / emitters on `ctx.heroFX` alone.

## Gate correctly

| Concern                                                                       | Gate                                                                                                                                    |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Attack, jump, zap, missiles, operate, emitters, hit sounds for those          | `UseContext.canWorldFx(ch)` / `ctx.canWorldFx()` (`sprite != null && parent != null`) — often **body**; use **kit** after sprite borrow |
| QuickSlot, GLog, identify, talent UI, `spendAndNext`, camera-only Hero riders | `ctx.heroFX`                                                                                                                            |

```java
// ❌ BAD — Echo never swings / never bolts
if (ctx.heroFX && kit.sprite != null) {
	kit.sprite.attack(enemy.pos, doHit);
} else {
	doHit.call();
}

// ✅ GOOD — Hero: anim then hit; on-stage Echo: visual + sync hit (borrow-safe); headless: sync only
if (ctx.heroFX && UseContext.canWorldFx(kit)) {
	kit.sprite.attack(enemy.pos, doHit);
} else {
	if (UseContext.canWorldFx(kit)) {
		kit.sprite.attack(enemy.pos); // visual only
	}
	doHit.call();
}
```

Relocates: `Char.move(cell, false)` or `ScrollOfTeleportation.appear` — not `pos` alone.

## Tests

Prefer proving Echo VFX with a live parent — skill `echo-combat-vfx-test`:
`installEchoBossLevel` + `attachInstantProjectileParent`, then assert recycles / stub counters.

Headless (no parent) must still apply gameplay synchronously.

